      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Common Milestone 2 approach: it is easier to first implement and verify the parallel model on CPU before progressing to a scaled-up GPU implementation. Since a GPU is much faster than a CPU, parallelised CPU code can appropriately support the GPU for once-off routines at the start/finish of the simulation that are too difficult or tedious for GPU but still computationally intensive enough to warrant an optimised CPU implementation.",
